The graph of $y = 2-\sqrt{3}\tan x$ and the line $y = 3$ are shown for $0 \le x \le 2\pi$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-0.3, xmax=6.9, ymin=-6.5, ymax=10.5,
  xtick={1.5708, 3.1416, 4.7124, 6.2832},
  xticklabels={$\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$, $\frac{3\pi}{2}$, $2\pi$},
  ytick={-4, 3, 8},
  samples=100, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-6.5:10.5, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=11cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=0:1.3573] {2-1.73205*tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=1.7843:4.4989] {2-1.73205*tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=4.9259:6.2832] {2-1.73205*tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[thick, red, domain=0:6.2832] {3};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Solve $2-\sqrt{3}\tan x = 3$ for $0 \le x \le 2\pi$.
